From 9354412d589a23f73abc4ba37b87d9ff28fc5f4f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cristian Papa <pcristian292@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 19:55:44 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: xpon: restart the GPON session when the OMCI
 agent is toggled

Disabling the OMCI agent marks it not operational, and the PON netdev
loses its carrier. Enabling it again only makes it operational once it
answers an OLT request. An OLT that has already provisioned the ONU, and
still sees it in O5, sends none, so the carrier stays down until a
reboot.

Restart the session when agent-enabled changes, as for the other keys
that define it. The OLT then ranges and provisions the ONU again, and
the agent becomes operational on its first answer.

On an Archer XR500v on a Huawei OLT, the agent disabled and enabled
again from LuCI left the link at "O5=1 OMCI=0" for minutes. One session
restart brought it back: O5 after 7 seconds, link ready after 8, and the
WAN session up 5 seconds later.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Cristian Papa <pcristian292@gmail.com>
Signed-off-by: Matheus Sampaio Queiroga <srherobrine20@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_xpon.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_xpon.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_xpon.c
index 63d881bcd..bf56f7ff4 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_xpon.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_xpon.c
@@ -1848,6 +1848,13 @@ void airoha_gpon_omci_hw_set_operational(void *hw_priv, bool operational)
 static bool airoha_gpon_config_requires_restart(u16 key)
 {
 	switch (key) {
+	/*
+	 * Not a live policy toggle: disabling the agent takes the service
+	 * down, and once enabled again it only becomes operational when the
+	 * OLT next sends a request. An OLT that has already provisioned the
+	 * ONU sends none, so the link would stay down until a reboot.
+	 */
+	case OMCI_CONFIG_AGENT_ENABLED:
 	case OMCI_CONFIG_SERIAL_NUMBER:
 	case OMCI_CONFIG_VENDOR_ID:
 	case OMCI_CONFIG_VERSION:
-- 
2.55.0

